{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>ויגש אליו יהודה</b> In gematria this is to do battle with Joseph, and in gematria also he entered for appeasement, for three things he entered (and see Rashi):" "<b> ויגש אליו יהודה</b> ס\"ת שוה — he said to him: I am your equal, for just as you are a king, so too I am a king. And on this the Midrash expounds: \"For behold, the kings were arrayed\" (Psalms 2:2)." "<b> בי אדני</b> Meaning: by me, do whatever you desire, and the lad will go up with his brothers." "<b> ואל יחר</b> Two times in the Masorah: here, and the other: ואל יחר בעיניכם כי מכרתם אותי הנה כי למחיה שלחני אלהים לפניכם (Genesis 45:5). And we expound: teaches that their faces changed like the blackened bottom of a pot — for upon whom did they have to be incensed? So too Judah said to him: let not your face change, I need to speak a little." "<b> כמוך כפרעה</b> In gematria: בך אתחיל."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:23.444028957Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}